# ============================================================================
#  .gitignore  --  "things git should pretend do not exist"
# ============================================================================
#
#  EXPERT: Git tracks files. Anything matching a pattern in this file is left
#          untracked, so build junk and local secrets never get committed.
#  KID:    This is the list of toys we do NOT put in our school bag: the mess
#          we make while building, and the secret diary only we may read.
# ============================================================================

# `target/` is where Cargo puts every compiled artefact. It is huge, machine
# specific, and fully reproducible from source -- never commit it.
/target

# Backup files some editors leave behind when saving a Rust file.
**/*.rs.bk

# Local runtime data created while testing the daemon by hand.
# (Real deployments put this in /etc/otkp, which is outside the repo anyway.)
/otkp-data/

# Working notes that are deliberately local-only: session plans, resume specs,
# scratch design thinking. Not for publication, so not tracked.
/.hermes/

# NOTE: We deliberately DO commit `Cargo.lock`.
# For a *binary* crate, the lock file pins exact dependency versions, which is
# how you get reproducible, auditable builds. (For a *library* you would ignore
# it, so downstream users can pick their own versions.)
